R&C patch 2173 (a4o-gpuwait, 2026-11-24): chunk submits split an open ZPASS query into host segments.

Patch 2029 submits the walker's command list every LD_SUBMIT_CHUNK (128) draws so the GPU runs behind the walker, but it
refused while an occlusion query was open (D3D12 needs Begin and End in one list; a split query made patch 2025 count
two segments, which a GET_REPORT turns into OQ_ALWAYS). A4O Luminopolis fires 25-31 chunks per frame against ~70
expected and one list holds 31-60 ms of GPU work ([perf-gpu] longest, gpuprof-1124 run): the GPU idles while the walker
records, then the walker waits for the whole list (design: work/coord/blockers-1124/a4o-gpuwait/design.md).

Now (LD_OQ_SPLIT=1, default) a chunk submit ends the open query, submits, and begins a new query ("host segment") in the
next list. The title's game segment (2025's segment) is the contiguous run of host segments [first_serial, last_serial];
segs still counts game segments only, so every report state (NEVER / PENDING / ALWAYS) is decided as before (states
and counts are the same; the frame a count lands in can be earlier, as each entry carries an earlier chunk fence). A PENDING
report's count is the sum of its k host segments: the 2027 readback queues k entries (one ResolveQueryData per run
contiguous in both the query heap and the readback ring) and ld_rb_drain sums them, saturated, into one guest write; a
predicated draw (SET_RENDER_ENABLE mode 2) of a k > 1 report gets pred[slot] = the sum from a one-thread compute pass
(ld_oq_prepare_draw, run before the draw's state memo check). k == 1 is the old path line for line. If the sum pass
cannot be built, such a report draws unconditionally (2025's answer for a split query), logged once and counted.
LD_OQ_SPLIT=0 keeps the refusal (A/B). LD_OQ_SPLIT=2 (opt-in, a behaviour change: needs its own RPCS3-referenced A/B)
also continues a game segment across a flush, so reports that fall to ALWAYS today get real counts.

The bookkeeping is in libs/video/rsx_oq_split.h (no D3D12). Counters: one [perf-oq] line per second inside the
RSX_PERF_PROF window (mode, host splits, chunk submits refused under an open query, flushes that closed a game segment,
draws per game segment mean/max, reports, split reports, largest k, sum passes and fallbacks, the 2025 counters and the
2027 readback counters as period deltas). Host test: R&C port/rc/tests/run_oq_split_test.sh (red without this patch,
two mutants caught). Not yet run in the game: the A/B is plan.json a4o steps save-luminopolis-oqsplit-off/-on.

